# ROAD RUBBLE: what is left of a destroyed road piece - broken paving stones, low and flat (no pile: a body walks over
# it). One object, `RubbleRoad`, inside +-0.95 m of the origin; the origin is on the GROUND (y = 0 is the bottom).
# Written by hand. Every piece is an axis-aligned box with flat facets: 8 positions a piece, the faces name them
# RELATIVE (-8 .. -1), and all pieces share one UV and these six normals: 1 +X  2 -X  3 +Y  4 -Y  5 +Z  6 -Z
vt 0.5 0.5
vn 1 0 0
vn -1 0 0
vn 0 1 0
vn 0 -1 0
vn 0 0 1
vn 0 0 -1

o RubbleRoad
